 "summary": "Checked every new definition and theorem against standard radiative-DIS kinematics: the hard-scattering record, the collinear-ISR relations (Q\u00b2 = zQ\u00b2_e, 1-y_e = z(1-y), x_e = xy/(1-z(1-y))), the Sigma-method exactness in (x,y), the collinear-FSR relation Q\u00b2_e = zQ\u00b2 - (1-z)k\u00b2, and both bilinear-form expansions all verify by hand, including degenerate/junk-value branches. The roadmap-mandated Q\u00b2_\u03a3 := Q\u00b2_e deviates from Bassler-Bernardi and blocks the (x,Q\u00b2) form of acceptance example 3, but it matches README 1.2 verbatim and is flagged honestly in the docstring and PR description, so it is a human roadmap decision rather than a defect here.",
